<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Layout xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE <Layout>
         breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
         xml file" error.

         BUSINESS FIELDS ADDED 2026-08-20 (UAT gap). Until now this layout was a STUB: it carried
         exactly four fields, Name, OwnerId, CreatedById and LastModifiedById, and not one business
         field. This is the third of the three disposition child layouts found empty in the same UAT
         pass, alongside BOV_Submission__c and Disposition_Offer__c.

         WHY IT SURVIVED TO UAT: every read path bypasses layouts. BrokerListingSelector names its
         columns in SOQL and lwc/brokerListing renders them itself, so the listing card looked
         complete while the create and detail screens were empty.

         🔴 THE SYMPTOM DIFFERS FROM ITS TWO SIBLINGS, AND THAT IS WORTH KNOWING BEFORE ANYONE
         RETESTS. Nothing navigates to a standard "new Broker Listing" modal: lwc/brokerListing has
         no NavigationMixin create call, and the record is created in Apex by
         DispositionStageEntryService, which stamps Listing_Status__c to its initial value. So the
         empty layout was never blocking a CREATE here the way "+ Log Offer" was; it was blanking
         the DETAIL and EDIT screens of a record the service had already made. Disposition__c is
         placed below anyway, because a lookup absent from the layout is invisible on the detail
         page and cannot be repaired by hand if the service ever links the wrong parent.

         BEHAVIOUR RULES APPLIED:
         1. NO FORMULA FIELDS EXIST ON THIS OBJECT. All nine custom fields were checked in
            objects/Broker_Listing__c/fields/; none carries a formula element.
         2. NO MACHINE OWNED FIELD EXISTS ON THIS OBJECT EITHER, so every business field below is
            Edit. This was verified, not assumed: the only Apex write to any field on this object is
            DispositionStageEntryService setting Listing_Status__c at creation, and a one time
            initial value is not the same thing as an automation that owns the field for its
            lifetime. Days_On_Market__c and Offers_Received__c in particular LOOK derived and are
            NOT: no Apex, trigger or Flow writes either one, and both are only ever read, so
            locking them would leave them permanently at their default. Offers_Received__c is a
            plain Number with defaultValue 0, not a roll up summary.
         3. Name stays Readonly. It is an AutoNumber, displayFormat BL-{0000}.

         THIS OBJECT HAS NO APPROVAL PROCESS, so unlike its two siblings it correctly has no
         relatedLists block and no RelatedProcessHistoryList. Nothing was removed. -->
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>false</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>false</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Information</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Readonly</behavior>
                <field>Name</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Disposition__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Broker_Firm__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Contact_Name__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Listing_Status__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>OwnerId</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>TwoColumnsTopToBottom</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>true</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>true</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Listing Terms and Timeline</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>List_Date__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Call_For_Offers_Date__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Commission_Percent__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Days_On_Market__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Edit</behavior>
                <field>Offers_Received__c</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>TwoColumnsTopToBottom</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>false</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>false</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>System Information</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Readonly</behavior>
                <field>CreatedById</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Readonly</behavior>
                <field>LastModifiedById</field>
            </layoutItems>
        </layoutColumns>
        <style>TwoColumnsTopToBottom</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>false</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>false</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <layoutColumns/>
        <style>CustomLinks</style>
    </layoutSections>
    <showEmailCheckbox>false</showEmailCheckbox>
    <showHighlightsPanel>false</showHighlightsPanel>
    <showInteractionLogPanel>false</showInteractionLogPanel>
    <showRunAssignmentRulesCheckbox>false</showRunAssignmentRulesCheckbox>
    <showSubmitAndAttachButton>false</showSubmitAndAttachButton>
</Layout>
